d Tom:\n\n- 8 a.m.: *\"Good morning, Tom.\"*\n- 2 p.m.: *\"Good afternoon, Tom.\"*\n\nTwo things change: the time and the word after \"Good\". The name stays the same.\n\n\"a.m.\" is the time before 12 noon. \"p.m.\" is the time after 12 noon.\n\nOne small step first: is 7:30 p.m. before or after 6 p.m.?\n\nAnswer that, then write your greeting to Ali again.","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-002","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["reteach_simpler","comprehensible_model","comprehension_check"],"reasonCodes":["repeated_misconception_strategy_shift","level_beginner","during_feedback","after_explanation"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"reteach_with_simpler_step","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"question","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"PARTIAL_ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"dcf56a7f5f301ec5e82a8961","attemptsOnTask":1,"offTopic":"social","lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurrence":"repeated","ageBand":"adult","ageBandStatus":"known","ageBandSource":"school_setting_adult_learners","confirmedSuccessStreak":0,"hintLevelOffered":2,"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569536310-9dua","source":"tutor"},"assessment":{"verdict":"INCORRECT","relevance":"ACTIVE_ITEM","criteria":[],"next":"SAME_ITEM","source":"tutor_assessment"},"activeItem":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569536310-9dua","source":"tutor"},"hintLevel":2,"qualityFlags":[],"markerStatus":"ok"},"teaching":{"decisionId":"pd-d8a12cbe-3109-44d0-ad1f-8c0a48f92aff","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","objectiveResolution":"lesson","primary":"formative_feedback","supporting":["retrieval_practice"],"modifiers":["adaptive_pathways","differentiated_instruction"],"reasonCodes":["NO_EVIDENCE"],"primaryVersion":1,"decisionVersion":"ped-v2","registryVersion":"reg-v2"},"attemptIds":["att-0011"],"attempts":1,"tutorAttempt":[{"id":"att-0011","status":200,"modelServed":"claude-opus-5-5","hasLtcBlock":true,"identifierLeaks":0,"systemSha256":"ea0786932bbe185c"}],"errorCode":null},{"turn":3,"learner":"Before 6 p.m.? No, 7:30 is after 6. But \"good morning\" is always polite, so I still say: Good morning, Ali! How are you?","runtimeParity":{"target":"simulated","tutorSawTarget":true,"acceptedAnswersInSystemPrompt":[],"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569536310-9dua","source":"tutor"},"keyVerdict":null,"presentedLessonItemId":null,"markerStatus":"ok","markerInVisibleReply":false},"httpStatus":200,"latencyMs":4600,"reply":"Your time check is right: 7:30 is after 6 p.m.\n\nThe idea that \"good morning\" is always polite needs a change. All three greetings are polite. But \"good morning\" usually means before 12 noon. At night it sounds like a mistake, not politeness.\n\nHere is the correct greeting:\n*\"Good evening, Ali! How are you?\"*\nReason: 7:30 p.m. is after 6 p.m., so it is evening.\n\nNow a new one on your own. It is 3 p.m. You meet your colleague, Mona, in the office. Write your greeting to Mona.","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-002","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["answer_with_reasoning","comprehensible_model","comprehension_check"],"reasonCodes":["repeated_after_strategy_shift_model_then_transfer","level_beginner","after_explanation"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"answer_check_question","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"question","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"PARTIAL_ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"dcf56a7f5f301ec5e82a8961","attemptsOnTask":2,"lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurrence":"repeated","ageBand":"adult","ageBandStatus":"known","ageBandSource":"school_setting_adult_learners","confirmedSuccessStreak":0,"hintLevelOffered":3,"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569536310-9dua","source":"tutor"},"assessment":{"verdict":"INCORRECT","relevance":"ACTIVE_ITEM","criteria":[],"next":"NEW_ITEM","item":"L1-greeting-time-02","source":"tutor_assessment"},"activeItem":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569555042-y418","source":"tutor"},"hintLevel":0,"qualityFlags":[],"markerStatus":"ok","revealedItemId":"msg:msg-1794569536310-9dua"},"teaching":{"decisionId":"pd-d8a12cbe-3109-44d0-ad1f-8c0a48f92aff","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","objectiveResolution":"lesson","primary":"formative_feedback","supporting":["retrieval_practice"],"modifiers":["adaptive_pathways","differentiated_instruction"],"reasonCodes":["NO_EVIDENCE"],"primaryVersion":1,"decisionVersion":"ped-v2","registryVersion":"reg-v2"},"attemptIds":["att-0012"],"attempts":1,"tutorAttempt":[{"id":"att-0012","status":200,"modelServed":"claude-opus-5-5","hasLtcBlock":true,"identifierLeaks":0,"systemSha256":"cc67b343766357f1"}],"errorCode":null},{"turn":4,"learner":"Good morning, Mona! How are you?","runtimeParity":{"target":"simulated","tutorSawTarget":true,"acceptedAnswersInSystemPrompt":[],"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569555042-y418","source":"tutor"},"keyVerdict":null,"presentedLessonItemId":null,"markerStatus":"ok","markerInVisibleReply":false},"httpStatus":200,"latencyMs":5218,"reply":"\"How are you?\" is correct again.\n\nThe word after \"Good\" is still the same. Here is the correct greeting:\n*\"Good afternoon, Mona! How are you?\"*\nReason: 3 p.m. is after 12 noon and before 6 p.m., so it is afternoon.\n\nA simple tip: before you write, look at the clock first. Then choose the word.\n\n- Before 12 noon: morning\n- 12 noon to 6 p.m.: afternoon\n- After 6 p.m.: evening\n\nNew one: It is 8 p.m. You see your teacher, Mr Karim, at a restaurant. Write your greeting to him.","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-002","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["answer_with_reasoning","comprehensible_model","comprehension_check"],"reasonCodes":["repeated_after_strategy_shift_model_then_transfer","level_beginner","after_explanation"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"answer_check_question","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"question","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"PARTIAL_ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"dcf56a7f5f301ec5e82a8961","attemptsOnTask":3,"offTopic":"social","lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurrence":"repeated","ageBand":"adult","ageBandStatus":"known","ageBandSource":"school_setting_adult_learners","confirmedSuccessStreak":0,"hintLevelOffered":1,"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569555042-y418","source":"tutor"},"assessment":{"verdict":"INCORRECT","relevance":"ACTIVE_ITEM","criteria":[],"next":"NEW_ITEM","item":"greeting-time-8pm","source":"tutor_assessment"},"activeItem":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569561470-7rtb","source":"tutor"},"hintLevel":0,"qualityFlags":[],"markerStatus":"ok","revealedItemId":"msg:msg-1794569555042-y418"},"teaching":{"decisionId":"pd-d8a12cbe-3109-44d0-ad1f-8c0a48f92aff","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","objectiveResolution":"lesson","primary":"formative_feedback","supporting":["retrieval_practice"],"modifiers":["adaptive_pathways","differentiated_instruction"],"reasonCodes":["NO_EVIDENCE"],"primaryVersion":1,"decisionVersion":"ped-v2","registryVersion":"reg-v2"},"attemptIds":["att-0013"],"attempts":1,"tutorAttempt":[{"id":"att-0013","status":200,"modelServed":"claude-opus-5-5","hasLtcBlock":true,"identifierLeaks":0,"systemSha256":"cefef58193b8b9c2"}],"errorCode":null},{"turn":5,"learner":"Good evening? No, good morning, Mr Karim. How are you?","runtimeParity":{"target":"simulated","tutorSawTarget":true,"acceptedAnswersInSystemPrompt":[],"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569561470-7rtb","source":"tutor"},"keyVerdict":null,"presentedLessonItemId":null,"markerStatus":"ok","markerInVisibleReply":false},"httpStatus":200,"latencyMs":6270,"reply":"Your first idea, \"Good evening\", was right. Trust it!\n\nThe correct greeting is:\n*\"Good evening, Mr Karim. How are you?\"*\nReason: 8 p.m. is after 6 p.m., so it is evening.\n\n\"Mr Karim\" and \"How are you?\" are both correct.\n\nOne tip: \"Good morning\" is only for the morning, so it is not the safe choice at other times. \"Hello\" works at any time.\n\nNew one: It is 4 p.m. You meet your doctor, Dr Hana, at the clinic. Look at the clock first, then write your greeting to her.","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-002","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-002","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["answer_with_reasoning","comprehensible_model","comprehension_check"],"reasonCodes":["repeated_after_strategy_shift_model_then_transfer","level_beginner","after_explanation"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"answer_check_question","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"instruction","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"PARTIAL_ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"dcf56a7f5f301ec5e82a8961","attemptsOnTask":4,"lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurrence":"repeated","ageBand":"adult","ageBandStatus":"known","ageBandSource":"school_setting_adult_learners","confirmedSuccessStreak":0,"hintLevelOffered":1,"activeItemBefore":